# dependencies / build output
node_modules/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# virtualenvs (backend/venv and backend/myenv already exist locally and are
# Python 3.13 builds — this project pins to Python 3.12, see README)
venv/
myenv/
.venv/
env/
# data + generated index (never commit the dataset or secrets)
backend/data/
backend/index/
index/
.env
# ...and any archive of that data. backend/data/ is ignored, but a zip of it
# sitting anywhere else is not, and that zip is how the dataset gets handed to a
# new teammate (HANDOFF.md step 2) -- so it is routinely in the working tree.
*.zip
# Terraform. State is not source code: it records live infrastructure, including
# the cluster's CA certificate and resource IDs, and a saved plan file embeds the
# whole state as well. `.terraform/` is 120 MB of downloaded provider binaries.
# The lock file IS committed on purpose -- it pins the provider version that was
# actually applied.
deploy/terraform/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
tfplan
tfplan-*
crash.log
